IMPORT prelude

-- Co-operative Societies Act 1979 (Singapore) -- what a member, a committee member and a society meet: founding numbers (s 5),
-- who may join (s 39), one member one vote (s 42), the 20% shareholding cap (s 43), share transfers (s 44(2)), the two-year tail of a
-- past member's liability (s 47), withdrawal notice (s 48), expulsion (s 49(1)), the annual general meeting and its notice (s 53),
-- requisitioned meetings (s 55(2)), quorum and voting (ss 56, 57), who may sit on the committee (s 60(1), (3), (4)), the levy on
-- surplus (s 71(2), (2A)), bonus certificates and bonus shares (s 73(3), (5)), and the word "co-operative" (s 99).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/CSA1979.txt. The deposit labels
-- itself as incorporating amendments up to 1 December 2021; later amendments are annotated in the body, the latest seen being
-- Act 5 of 2025 (wef 9 March 2025).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 4 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the rules with numbers in them that
-- members and officers of a society actually meet. Not encoded: registration procedure and the Registrar's discretion (ss 6-10A),
-- by-laws, credit-society conversion and control (ss 16A-16BB), records, audit and returns (ss 31-37), loans, borrowing and
-- investment (ss 67-70), dividends capped by Rules (s 72), amalgamation, inquiry, dissolution and liquidation (Parts 7-8), disputes
-- (s 91), the general offences of ss 100-100F, and anything left to the Rules or written directions.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions as seen in the example rows. No pipeline,
-- no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Co-operative Societies Act 1979 -- members and meetings`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `5 -- founding numbers`

-- s 5(1): a primary society cannot be registered "unless it consists of at least 5 persons, each of whom qualifies for membership
-- under section 39(1)". (2): a secondary society needs "2 or more persons, each being a society, a trade union or a platform work
-- association".
GIVEN `qualified founders` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a primary society has enough founders` IF
    `qualified founders` AT LEAST 5

GIVEN `institutional founders` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a secondary society has enough founders` IF
    `institutional founders` AT LEAST 2

§§ `39 -- who may join a primary society`

-- s 39(1)(a): an individual must have "attained 16 years of age or, if the society is a school co-operative, has attained 12 years
-- of age"; be "a citizen of Singapore or ... resident in Singapore"; and meet the by-laws' other requirements. (7): a member found
-- disqualified "ceases to be a member". The credit-society common bond of s 39(4)-(6) is not encoded.
GIVEN `age` IS A NUMBER, `school co-operative` IS A BOOLEAN, `citizen or resident` IS A BOOLEAN, `meets the by-laws` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the individual qualifies for membership` IF
        (IF `school co-operative` THEN `age` AT LEAST 12 ELSE `age` AT LEAST 16)
    AND `citizen or resident`
    AND `meets the by-laws`

§§ `42 -- one member, one vote`

-- s 42(1): each individual member of a primary society "has only one vote ... irrespective of the number of shares the member
-- holds and that vote must be exercised in person and not by proxy".
GIVEN `shares held` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the votes of an individual member of a primary society` MEANS 1

§§ `43, 44 -- holding and transferring shares`

-- s 43(1): "a member cannot hold more than 20% of the share capital of a society", (2) unless the Registrar grants written approval;
-- (3) the section "does not apply to a member that is a society, a trade union or a platform work association".
GIVEN `percent of share capital` IS A NUMBER, `Registrar approved` IS A BOOLEAN, `member is an institution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the holding breaches the cap` IF
        `percent of share capital` GREATER THAN 20
    AND (NOT `Registrar approved`)
    AND (NOT `member is an institution`)

-- s 44(2): no transfer unless "(a) the member has held that share or interest for at least one year; and (b) the transfer or charge
-- is in favour of the society, a member of the society or a person ... whose application for membership has been accepted by the
-- committee of management".
GIVEN `years held` IS A NUMBER, `transferee is the society, a member or an accepted applicant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the share may be transferred` IF
    `years held` AT LEAST 1 AND `transferee is the society, a member or an accepted applicant`

§§ `47, 48, 49 -- leaving`

-- s 47(1): a past member's liability for the society's debts as they stood when membership ceased "does not continue for a period
-- of more than 2 years after that date". (2) the same for a deceased member's estate, from the date of death.
GIVEN `years since ceasing to be a member` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the past member is still liable` IF
    `years since ceasing to be a member` AT MOST 2

-- s 48: withdrawal on the notice the by-laws prescribe, except that "(a) in the case of a primary society, the notice must not exceed
-- one year; and (b) in the case of a secondary society or an apex organisation, the notice must not exceed 2 years".
GIVEN `primary society` IS A BOOLEAN, `months of notice required by the by-laws` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the required withdrawal notice is lawful` IF
    IF `primary society`
    THEN `months of notice required by the by-laws` AT MOST 12
    ELSE `months of notice required by the by-laws` AT MOST 24

-- s 49(1): expulsion "by a vote of at least two-thirds of the members present and voting at a general meeting upon a charge of which
-- the member is informed in writing by the committee of management at least one week before the meeting". (2) by-laws may provide a
-- different procedure; that alternative is not encoded.
GIVEN `votes to expel` IS A NUMBER, `members present and voting` IS A NUMBER, `days of written notice of the charge` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the expulsion is carried under s 49(1)` IF
    `votes to expel` TIMES 3 AT LEAST `members present and voting` TIMES 2
    AND `days of written notice of the charge` AT LEAST 7

§§ `53, 55 -- calling meetings`

-- s 53(1): an annual general meeting "within 6 months after the end of the society's financial year or such longer period as the
-- Registrar may allow". (3): notice "at least 15 clear days before the date of the meeting", unless the by-laws provide longer.
GIVEN `months after year end` IS A NUMBER, `Registrar allowed longer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the AGM is late` IF
    `months after year end` GREATER THAN 6 AND (NOT `Registrar allowed longer`)

GIVEN `clear days of notice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the general meeting notice meets the statutory minimum` IF
    `clear days of notice` AT LEAST 15

-- s 55(2): an extraordinary general meeting "must be convened ... on receipt of a requisition ... signed by at least 20% or 60 of the
-- members or delegates of the society, whichever is the less". (3): if not convened within one month, the requisitionists may.
GIVEN `members` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the requisition threshold` MEANS
    `the lesser of` (`members` TIMES 0.2) 60

GIVEN `signatures` IS A NUMBER, `members` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the committee must convene an EGM` IF
    `signatures` AT LEAST `the requisition threshold` `members`

§§ `56, 57 -- quorum and voting`

-- s 56(1): "The quorum ... is 20% or 30 of all members or delegates qualified to vote, whichever is the less." (2): if no quorum
-- within 30 minutes, "the members or delegates present form a quorum", but (a) that meeting cannot amend the by-laws and (b) a
-- resolution needs "a majority of two-thirds of the members or delegates present".
-- s 57(1): otherwise "a majority of votes"; (2) "In the case of an equality of votes, the motion is held to be lost"; (3) no
-- casting vote.
GIVEN `members` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the quorum` MEANS
    `the lesser of` (`members` TIMES 0.2) 30

GIVEN `present` IS A NUMBER, `members` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a full quorum is present` IF
    `present` AT LEAST `the quorum` `members`

GIVEN `present` IS A NUMBER, `members` IS A NUMBER, `minutes waited` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the meeting may transact business` IF
    `a full quorum is present` `present` `members` OR `minutes waited` GREATER THAN 30

GIVEN `present` IS A NUMBER, `members` IS A NUMBER, `minutes waited` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the meeting may amend the by-laws` IF
    `a full quorum is present` `present` `members`

GIVEN `votes for` IS A NUMBER, `votes against` IS A NUMBER, `present` IS A NUMBER, `members` IS A NUMBER, `minutes waited` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the ordinary resolution passes` IF
    IF `a full quorum is present` `present` `members`
    THEN `votes for` GREATER THAN `votes against`
    ELSE `minutes waited` GREATER THAN 30 AND `votes for` TIMES 3 AT LEAST `present` TIMES 2

§§ `60 -- who may sit on the committee of management`

-- s 60(1): an individual is not eligible for, or to remain on, the committee if (a) below 12 (school co-operative) or 18 (other);
-- (b) "except with the Registrar's written approval", not "(i) a citizen of Singapore; or (ii) ... resident in Singapore"; (c) an
-- undischarged bankrupt (Singapore or foreign court); (d) "convicted of an offence under this Act"; (e) "dismissed as an employee of
-- a society"; (f) except with written approval, previously removed or suspended by the Registrar under s 94(1) or 94A(1).
-- s 60(3): a conviction elsewhere "involving fraud or dishonesty" bars a NON-CREDIT society's committee, except with approval, until
-- 5 years after release from prison (if imprisoned) or for 5 years from conviction (if not). (4): for a CREDIT society the bar has no
-- time limit, except with approval.
-- Reading s 60(1)(b) as barring an individual who is neither a citizen nor a resident is an inference from "is not -- (i) ... or
-- (ii)". Only one approval flag is modelled; it cures only (b), (f), (3) and (4), as the text says. The High Court's power to shorten
-- the s 60(3)(b) period is not encoded.
DECLARE Candidate HAS
    `age` IS A NUMBER
    `school co-operative` IS A BOOLEAN
    `citizen or resident` IS A BOOLEAN
    `undischarged bankrupt` IS A BOOLEAN
    `convicted under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `dismissed by a society` IS A BOOLEAN
    `removed or suspended by the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
    `convicted of fraud or dishonesty elsewhere` IS A BOOLEAN
    `years since release or conviction` IS A NUMBER
    `credit society` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has the Registrar's written approval` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `c` IS A Candidate
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the fraud bar applies` IF
        `c`'s `convicted of fraud or dishonesty elsewhere`
    AND (NOT `c`'s `has the Registrar's written approval`)
    AND (`c`'s `credit society` OR `c`'s `years since release or conviction` LESS THAN 5)

GIVEN `c` IS A Candidate
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the candidate may sit on the committee` IF
        (IF `c`'s `school co-operative` THEN `c`'s `age` AT LEAST 12 ELSE `c`'s `age` AT LEAST 18)
    AND (`c`'s `citizen or resident` OR `c`'s `has the Registrar's written approval`)
    AND (NOT `c`'s `undischarged bankrupt`)
    AND (NOT `c`'s `convicted under this Act`)
    AND (NOT `c`'s `dismissed by a society`)
    AND ((NOT `c`'s `removed or suspended by the Registrar`) OR `c`'s `has the Registrar's written approval`)
    AND (NOT `the fraud bar applies` `c`)

§§ `71 -- the levy on surplus`

-- s 71(2): every society must contribute "(a) 5% ... of the first $500,000 of the surplus" to the Central Co-operative Fund and
-- "(b) 20% ... of any surplus in excess of $500,000" to that Fund "or to the Singapore Labour Foundation as the society may opt".
-- (2A): gains on disposal of (a) immovable property the society uses for its own operations, or (b) shares in any entity, "are
-- excluded from the surplus". Prescribed substitute rates, Government grants excluded by order (2B), and remission (6) are not
-- encoded.
GIVEN `surplus` IS A NUMBER, `excluded disposal gains` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the levied surplus` MEANS
    IF `surplus` MINUS `excluded disposal gains` LESS THAN 0 THEN 0 ELSE `surplus` MINUS `excluded disposal gains`

GIVEN `surplus` IS A NUMBER, `excluded disposal gains` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the contribution on the first $500,000` MEANS
    `the lesser of` (`the levied surplus` `surplus` `excluded disposal gains`) 500000 TIMES 0.05

GIVEN `surplus` IS A NUMBER, `excluded disposal gains` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the contribution on the excess` MEANS
    IF `the levied surplus` `surplus` `excluded disposal gains` GREATER THAN 500000
    THEN (`the levied surplus` `surplus` `excluded disposal gains` MINUS 500000) TIMES 0.2
    ELSE 0

GIVEN `surplus` IS A NUMBER, `excluded disposal gains` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the total contribution` MEANS
    `the contribution on the first $500,000` `surplus` `excluded disposal gains`
        PLUS `the contribution on the excess` `surplus` `excluded disposal gains`

§§ `73 -- bonus certificates and bonus shares`

-- s 73(3): holders of bonus certificates "are only entitled to claim payment out of the society's funds 5 years after the date when
-- the bonus certificates were issued"; (4) no interest or dividend on them. (5)(b): a bonus share under ordinary shares may be
-- withdrawn or transferred "only 10 years after the date when the bonus share was issued".
-- The early payout to a departing foreign worker or to the administrator of a dead or bankrupt member (s 73(7), (7A)) is not
-- encoded.
GIVEN `years since issue` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the bonus certificate may be cashed` IF
    `years since issue` AT LEAST 5

GIVEN `years since issue` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the bonus share may be withdrawn or transferred` IF
    `years since issue` AT LEAST 10

§§ `99 -- the word "co-operative"`

-- s 99(1): "No person other than a society may trade or carry on business under a name or title of which the word 'Co-operative' or
-- its equivalent in another language is part, without the Registrar's consent", saving a name used at 1 January 1980 by the person
-- or a successor in interest. (2): fine up to $5,000 and, for a continuing offence, "$500 for every day or part of a day during
-- which the offence continues after conviction".
GIVEN `is a society` IS A BOOLEAN, `Registrar consented` IS A BOOLEAN, `name in use at 1 January 1980` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `trading as co-operative is an offence` IF
    (NOT `is a society`) AND (NOT `Registrar consented`) AND (NOT `name in use at 1 January 1980`)

GIVEN `days continuing after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine under s 99` MEANS
    5000 PLUS 500 TIMES `days continuing after conviction`
